   "source": [
    "### What stands out\n",
    "\n",
    "1. The dataset contains **107,836 transactions** across six months, giving enough volume to compare categories and time patterns.\n",
    "2. **Electronics** contributes the largest revenue share, but it also shows the biggest January-to-June drop.\n",
    "3. **Apparel** moves upward over the same period, while **Grocery** is comparatively steady month to month.\n",
    "4. At product level, the report highlights **Smart TV** as the lowest-revenue Electronics product and **Saree / T-Shirt** as the leading Apparel products.\n",
    "5. Discount levels are worth checking carefully because average transaction revenue falls as the discount increases, while average units sold stay almost flat."
   ]
  },
