   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Category Manager Briefing\n",
    "\n",
    "### RENDLA PAVITHRA — TASK STARTED\n",
    "\n",
    "**Business Insights & Reporting:** Analyze the key findings, summarize **category performance and discount insights**, prepare **business recommendations**, and consolidate the final results for the presentation.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Business-focused interpretation of the analysis and key recommendations for the Category Manager.*\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Apparel shows the strongest growth opportunity.**  \n",
    "> Apparel revenue increased by **+34%**, growing from approximately **₹10.0M to ₹13.5M** over the six-month period. The consistent upward trend indicates an opportunity to give Apparel greater attention in terms of shelf allocation and promotional support.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Electronics requires closer performance monitoring.**  \n",
    "> Electronics remains the largest revenue-generating category, contributing approximately **49% of total revenue**. However, revenue declined from **₹45.7M in January to ₹29.7M in June**, a decrease of around **35%**. This downward trend needs further investigation before maintaining the same level of category allocation.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Discounting does not appear to increase transaction volume.**  \n",
    "> Across the observed discount levels, average units sold remain almost constant at approximately **2.58 units per transaction**, while revenue per transaction decreases as discounts increase. This suggests that higher discounts may be reducing revenue without creating a meaningful increase in sales volume.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Additional data is needed for a complete business decision.**  \n",
    "> The current analysis mainly focuses on revenue and sales data. Adding **COGS, profit margins, customer counts, and footfall data** would help evaluate the categories from a profitability perspective.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Technical observation:* Product-level differences within categories are relatively small compared with the larger category-level trends. The strongest signals in the dataset are therefore seen in **category performance and discount behaviour**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Summary of Core Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Primary Concern:** The overall revenue decline is strongly influenced by the reduction in **Electronics** revenue.\n",
    "- **Growth Opportunity:** **Apparel (+34%)** shows a consistent positive revenue trend and represents an area for further evaluation.\n",
    "- **Discount Insight:** Higher discounts do not show a corresponding increase in average units sold.\n",
    "- **Next Step:** Adding **COGS, margins, and customer-level metrics** can provide a more complete view of profitability and demand."
   ]
  }
